# cases the riscv32 column cannot serve: a case name or glob per line, then the reason.

* the riscv32 backend does not legalize 64-bit values, so no case can be built for it. every one refuses with "legalize: operation wider than the target ALU is unsupported (MIR_MOV, 8 bytes wide)", which is the first wide operation each case reaches: the fold accumulator the contract requires is a u64, so the move lands before anything else can. the register-pair lowering that closes it is the same work that would give this target an execution engine, so the column and the engine open together or not at all.
